          "type": "text",
          "text": "All four questions are answered by the source:\n\n1. **`__contains__`** returns `self.timer() < link.expires` — strict less-than, so at the exact deadline the entry is *not* visible.\n2. **`__getitem__`** on an expired key calls `self.__missing__(key)`, and `Cache.__missing__` just raises `KeyError` without touching stored data.\n3. **`__setitem__`** for an existing key unlinks its link and unconditionally sets `link.expires = time + self.__ttl`.\n4. **`expire()`** appends `(curr.key, cache_getitem(self, curr.key))` to `expired` and returns it.",
